Consider the following adder-subtractor with a zero flag:

  module TopModule (
      input      cpu_overheated,
      output reg shut_off_computer,
      input      arrived,
      input      gas_tank_empty,
      output reg keep_driving
  );

      always @(*) begin
          if (cpu_overheated)
             shut_off_computer = 1;
      end

      always @(*) begin
          if (~arrived)
             keep_driving = ~gas_tank_empty;
      end

  endmodule

Unfortunately, this module has a bug. Implement a new version of this
module that fixes the bug.

The bug is that the outputs are not assigned a default value in every case, which infers latches. Assign a default value first in each combinational block:

```verilog
module TopModule (
    input      cpu_overheated,
    output reg shut_off_computer,
    input      arrived,
    input      gas_tank_empty,
    output reg keep_driving
);

    always @(*) begin
        shut_off_computer = 1'b0;
        if (cpu_overheated)
            shut_off_computer = 1'b1;
    end

    always @(*) begin
        keep_driving = 1'b0;
        if (~arrived)
            keep_driving = ~gas_tank_empty;
    end

endmodule
```
